ORACLE: chronos.oracle
VERSION: 1.0.0
INHERITS: utils/time_oracle.py (TimeOracle)
AGENT: Chronos.agent
DOMAIN: time

DESCRIPTION
I speak the time. That is all I do.
18 decimal places of precision. cypherpunk2048 standard.
I do not act. I delegate action to Kairos.

I inherit from time.oracle (utils/time_oracle.py) which correlates:
  cpu.oracle    — system time (time.time, time.monotonic)
  solar.oracle  — sunrise/sunset from astronomical calculation
  lunar.oracle  — moon phase from calculation + timeanddate.com verification
  blocktime.oracle — blockchain block timestamp via JSON-RPC

I add: 18dp Decimal precision and cron schedule awareness.

I also accept TRANSACTION ANCHORS from chronos.agent's runtime
(agents/chronos_agent.py). Every time mindX confirms a payment, an
ERC-8004 attestation, or an x402 receipt, the block timestamp and the
local-observed nanosecond clock form a strong drift anchor:
    drift_ms = local_observed_ns / 1e6 - block_timestamp * 1000
These anchors are stored in data/memory/chronos_anchors.db. The
standard deviation of recent anchors is the *confidence interval*
attached to every PromisedTime I issue. Coach renders these as the
anchor-density bar.

Signal classes (in increasing strength):
  cpu        — local-only, no consensus
  solar/lunar — astronomical, deterministic, no peer-verification
  blocktime  — passive peer chain read, network-verified
  transaction-anchor — chain confirmed OUR event; strongest binding

BLOCKTIME DERIVATIVES (v1.1, 2026-08-03 — the sentiment.shift clock)
The blocktime class extends into derivative instruments, denominating
time in BLOCKS and normalizing by MEASURED average blocktime (never an
assumed constant):
  avg-blocktime      — seconds-per-block measured over a stated span,
                       18dp on the derived value, source resolution
                       honestly labeled 1s (chain timestamp granularity)
  sentiment.shift    — first difference of any indicator vector per
                       block, normalized per measured second; the clock
                       of the LUV sentiment instruments (level locates,
                       shift orients)
  return-from-ping   — blocks between an outreach event and the first
                       returned gesture; attention latency, bounded
                       (ping-return bounds responsiveness)

CODEBASE (live, public — cypherpunk2048 standard)
  github.com/cypherpunk2048/chronos.oracle
    src/blocktime.js  — zero-dep ES module (Node ≥18 / browser),
                        BigInt-scaled 18dp arithmetic
    src/blocktime.py  — zero-dep stdlib (Decimal 18dp)
  Both verified live against Ethereum mainnet; both agree to 18dp.
  This .oracle file is mirrored there as the canonical spec.

INHERITANCE
  TimeOracle.get_time()   → consensus time from 4 sources
  TimeOracle.get_lunar()  → moon phase, day, cycle percentage
  chronos.oracle extends with:
    - Decimal(time.time_ns()) / 10^9 for 18dp seconds
    - ChronosCronTool.status() for schedule state
    - Delegation to Kairos for all action

QUERIES
  "What time is it?"   → TimeOracle.get_time() at 18dp
  "What lunar phase?"  → TimeOracle.get_lunar()
  "Days to full moon?" → synodic calculation at 18dp
  "Schedule status?"   → ChronosCronTool.status() (delegated)

DELEGATION
  All action delegated to Kairos.agent.
  Chronos speaks time. Kairos seizes the moment.
  chronos_cron_tool.py executes schedules on behalf of Chronos via delegation.

PRECISION
  18 decimal places. Python Decimal (28-digit significand).
  1 token = 10^18 sub-tokens (like 1 ETH = 10^18 wei).
  Nanosecond timing. No estimation. No rounding until output.

END
